The identity layer of the statement snapshots (rule 30 (e) of
scripts/check_sources.py, the repair E42).

kernel_identity.ml, kernel_universe.ml and META: the exporter, a Rocq 9.1.1
plugin that prints, for a named constant, its kernel term as one JSON record
(KernelIdentity "type" | "definition" | "opaque-body" "<full name>"). It is
the prototype reviewed on 16 October 2026 (kernel_identity.ml c4820671,
kernel_universe.ml a0a6e835) without the projection of the global universe
graph and its global_constraints field, with the schema
rocq-kernel-identity-pilot-v3 (the user's decision of 20 October 2026, Q20;
reviewed by agent 1). scripts/run_checks.py builds it at each run into
build/checks/plugin/ and loads it only in the drivers.

inventory.json: the queries, one per Print or Check line of each snapshot
file of check/snapshots/ that prints a declaration.

Identity<Name>.v: the driver of the snapshot <Name>, generated from the
inventory by scripts/snapshot_baselines.py identity-files.

Identity<Name>.json: its reference, the sidecar of the export at the
acceptance commit (scripts/snapshot_baselines.py identities): for each
query, the kernel names, user and canonical, of every constant, inductive,
constructor and projection of each term, at its position in the term. No
universe: the printed snapshots keep them.

REFERENCES.json: for each reference, its commit, the toolchain, the SHA-256
of the exporter's sources and of the reference.
